---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Dotloop Integration Privacy Policy — Lu Zhang"
  description="Privacy policy for Lu Zhang's private Dotloop transaction-automation integration."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; max-width: 820px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Dotloop Integration Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This policy applies only to Lu Zhang's private Dotloop transaction-
      automation integration. It
      does not replace the general <a href="/privacy/">SciencesLoop Privacy Policy</a>
      or the separate property operations SMS policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Purpose and access</h2>
    <p>
      If Dotloop approves this integration and an authorized account holder
      explicitly connects an account through Dotloop OAuth, the integration may
      retrieve and process the authorized account, profile, loop, and
      transaction information for private property-operations workflows. The
      integration is not available to public site visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Approved transaction automation</h2>
    <p>
      Within Dotloop-approved API scopes and the authorized account/profile,
      the integration may automate approved transaction-management actions,
      such as creating or updating loops, synchronizing approved transaction
      fields, managing tasks and participants, and organizing or uploading
      documents. It will not sign documents or operate outside its approved
      workflow and permissions.
    </p>

    <h2>Use, retention, and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Dotloop information is used only for the authorized account holder's
      private operations workflows. It is not sold, publicly shared, or used
      for marketing. It is not sent to artificial-intelligence or
      machine-learning systems. Access credentials are stored outside the
      public website. Information is retained only to the extent necessary for
      the approved workflow or to meet an applicable legal obligation.
    </p>

    <h2>Control and contact</h2>
    <p>
      The authorized account holder can revoke the integration's access through Dotloop. For
      privacy questions or removal requests, contact
      <a href="mailto:luzhang@sciencesloop.com">luzhang@sciencesloop.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
